# clausal: no-collect
# The importer imports the owner's DUAL-DECLARED name ``t5b_kfact`` (an atom
# in the owner's -module list that also carries a /0 fact) and then writes
# clauses for ``t5b_kfact/2`` of its own.  Final review M-e refused this in
# the class era (the shared class put the owner's ``/0`` row in the write's
# blast radius).  Operator ruling 2026-09-24: a local p/2 beside an imported
# p/1 LOADS in both eras -- name and arity make a different predicate -- so
# this file now loads, and its t5b_kfact/2 is its own.  Loaded explicitly by
# tests/test_import_arity_resolution.py.
-module(t5b_dual_arity_clash, [t5b_dac_go(A, B)])
-import_from(tests.fixtures.t5b_dual_owner, [t5b_kfact])

t5b_kfact(1, 2),

t5b_dac_go(A, B) <- t5b_kfact(A, B),
